<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Can Germany overhaul its economy before AfD grows stronger?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:177cfd3f6546ebcbaf8bd947dca32420e4fa53c7cc6b56a3a6662a8dd7177b16</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-overhaul-its-economy-before-afd-grows-stronger/a-79696102--b0df844ba99a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-overhaul-its-economy-before-afd-grows-stronger/a-79696102?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflicts, rising costs and Chinese competition are testing Germany's economic model like never before. Which new sectors could revive growth and contain the far-right AfD, whose support has grown larger than ever?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany arrests Ukrainian man suspected of spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1026d9653e947ddbf9817cd52076c7c3ea444a37582db930486ad2d35379fa91</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-arrests-ukrainian-man-suspected-of-spying-for-russia/a-79732373--a3202cca0fcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-arrests-ukrainian-man-suspected-of-spying-for-russia/a-79732373?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The suspect is thought to have gathered defense-related information on the production of tanks and munitions, as well as details about NATO's eastern flank.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Government expecting increased tax revenue in 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d99855622997b4cd692b50065eedd19c46d1c1e029b745cfd3ab4a957a46505</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-government-expecting-increased-tax-revenue-in-2027/live-79728628--139a0de86753.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-government-expecting-increased-tax-revenue-in-2027/live-79728628?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finance Minister Lars Klingbeil said state tax revenue will increase by €4 billion in 2027. Meanwhile, public service websites have been coming back online after a PHP security scare. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German youth plan France-style mass protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2a6ccadc0935ba045cf760464b5213e994179d7ce7dcca4adc6de2715ace656</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T23:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-youth-plan-france-style-mass-protests/a-79727133--417332c907bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-youth-plan-france-style-mass-protests/a-79727133?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A youth-led movement in Germany has called for demonstrations in major cities of the country on October 31. The group has categorically distanced itself from the violence that took hold in France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: AfD's Weidel calls for major EU reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58a3025f9167e033de93413d28c7243695b746c2b6952e82f854508722bb6f5d</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-afd-s-weidel-calls-for-major-eu-reforms/live-79719483--29b68ddcd610.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-afd-s-weidel-calls-for-major-eu-reforms/live-79719483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right Alternative for Germany co-leader Alice Weidel reveals the party's plan to reform the EU. Meanwhile, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang was in Berlin to talk to developers and investors. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia arrests German man, calls him a Ukraine 'mercenary'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0fde8e8dad805a1bfedbd508212898825b668a131fad779924988fcddac951a</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871--8b55608360c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian FSB agents have arrested a German national and accused him of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine's military. They claim he deserted over unpaid wages and say he was a sniper who once served in the Bundeswehr.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD's Alice Weidel to unveil plan to cut EU powers — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c9f6d2cca5e19801af62b6c9e7e8cdbcc49fb1a7e351a2a7f9f342f19e4216a</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T22:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-s-alice-weidel-to-unveil-plan-to-cut-eu-powers-report/a-79717944--20fa5b0134f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-s-alice-weidel-to-unveil-plan-to-cut-eu-powers-report/a-79717944?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD will propose slashing powers of the European Union when it presents its policy paper on Wednesday, Politico reports.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Football: German coach Hürzeler flying high in Premier League</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fa4e5076b8a25f5135c4aada46a537e37d7c527766bd35a4b39f63255c53d9a</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-h_rzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763--701507a044eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-hürzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fabian Hürzeler is younger than his star player, a fellow Premier League German. But, contrary to his reputation in his homeland, Hürzeler has become a popular figure both on and off the pitch in England.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1c4a17104858ee9be801111eec1c5da027abd9daf4fc2dfb72f9d6edb16e75a</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why US investors are snapping up Germany's famed Mittelstand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35f64d41bd4688ab096452ca36a85e9fc8ea30b53d5cf0d5fe2329211190cc57</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T09:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421--453454d6f76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Increasing amounts of US capital are flowing into Germany's traditional industrial firms and family-owned businesses. As many business owners struggle to find successors, more companies are becoming acquisition targets.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224f082c59f6fe29f2c649ce513f9dada024dbce3912240b212e6fcb1bca78ac</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2982cfff49673da22c8690a6a13a8e5e149cbe8c5135dcf1fab0e65936f303c</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
